The sum of the numbers below eleven
  Lean     (Finset.range 11).sum id
  MeTTa    (Finset.sum (Nat.instAddCommMonoid) (Finset.range 11) itself)
  result   55
  checked  as a theorem of the Egal reading:
Theorem Lean_test_29 : (Lean_Finset_sum Lean_Nat Lean_Nat Lean_Nat_instAddCommMonoid (Lean_Finset_range (LeanNum 11)) (Sigma Lean_Nat (Lean_id Lean_Nat))) = (LeanNum 55).
  The statement's right side is the reading of the result.

How many numbers below twenty are multiples of three
  Lean     (Finset.filter (fun x => x % 3 = 0) (Finset.range 20)).card
  MeTTa    (Finset.card (Finset.filter multiple-of-three (Finset.range 20)))
  result   7
  checked  as a theorem of the Egal reading:
Theorem Lean_test_30 : (Lean_Finset_card Lean_Nat (Lean_Finset_filter Lean_Nat (fun v_x :e Lean_Nat => (Lean_Eq_Prop Lean_Nat (Lean_Nat_mod v_x (LeanNum 3)) (LeanNum 0))) (fun v_a :e Lean_Nat =>
    (Lean_instDecidableEqNat (Lean_Nat_mod v_a (LeanNum 3)) (LeanNum 0))) (Lean_Finset_range (LeanNum 20)))) = (LeanNum 7).
  The statement's right side is the reading of the result.

The first call cited with the theorem of the second
  Lean     (Finset.range 11).sum id
  MeTTa    (Finset.sum (Nat.instAddCommMonoid) (Finset.range 11) itself)
  result   55
  checked  as a theorem of the Egal reading:
Theorem Lean_test_30 : (Lean_Finset_card Lean_Nat (Lean_Finset_filter Lean_Nat (fun v_x :e Lean_Nat => (Lean_Eq_Prop Lean_Nat (Lean_Nat_mod v_x (LeanNum 3)) (LeanNum 0))) (fun v_a :e Lean_Nat =>
    (Lean_instDecidableEqNat (Lean_Nat_mod v_a (LeanNum 3)) (LeanNum 0))) (Lean_Finset_range (LeanNum 20)))) = (LeanNum 7).
  NOT THE SAME: the statement's right side is not the reading of the result.

